  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 137 PM EDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nNo significant updates for the extended period. The main story will \nbe rising temperatures and the potential for impactful heat by mid- \nto late this week. The set up responsible for these trends will be \nan eastward migrating mid-level ridge, currently over the Desert \nSouthwest and high pressure at the surface. Any disturbances that \ntranslate through the the mid/upper level flow may act to locally \nenhance convective activity on any given day. Otherwise, expect \ncontinued chances for daily afternoon/evening thunderstorms through \nthis next week. Temperatures are forecast to rise to the upper 80s \nto low 90s across most locations outside of the higher elevations. \nBy Wednesday, temperatures will trend upward a degree or two each \nday going forward. Increasing moisture will support the return of \ndewpoints in the mid- 70s and PwS in excess of 1.5\". Thus, heat \nindex values ('feels like' temperatures) are forecast to return to \nthe upper 90s to low 100s by mid to late week -- the highest values \ncurrently over parts of eastern GA. Heat headlines may be necessary \nin future forecasts. In the meantime, be mindful of the heat as you \nplan for any outdoor work or activities this coming week.",
